{
  "company_name": "MineTruck Analytics",
  "industry": "Mining",
  "use_case": "Haul vehicle asset health monitoring and predictive maintenance",
  "space_title": "MineTruck Analytics - Haul Vehicle Asset Health \ud83d\udd27",
  "space_description": "**Subindustry:** Mining\n\n**Use case:** Haul Vehicle Asset Health & Predictive Maintenance\n\nMineTruck Analytics \u2014 ultra-class haul truck reliability analytics across 20 Cat 797F / Komatsu 930E / Liebherr T284 / Hitachi EH5000 / BelAZ 75710 / Cat 794AC units operating across four pits. Mine Managers and Fleet Managers use this space to monitor daily availability, payload, and cycle time; Reliability VPs and CFOs use it to rank failure risk, plan component changeouts, and quantify unplanned downtime cost against a fleet replacement value of ~$5M per truck.\n\n**Key KPIs**\n- Mechanical availability (%) \u2014 target 85-92% for ultra-class trucks\n- Daily payload (tons) \u2014 total tons hauled per truck-day, typical range 100-400 tons across the fleet\n- Cycle time (minutes) \u2014 primary tons-per-operating-hour driver\n- Fleet health score (0-100) \u2014 composite from sensor telemetry\n- Critical / Warning alert count \u2014 leading indicator of unplanned downtime\n- Mean time between failures (MTBF, hours) \u2014 industry benchmark 200-400 hrs\n- Remaining useful life (RUL, days) \u2014 component changeout planning input\n- Repair cost ($) and unplanned downtime hours \u2014 opex and lost-production impact\n\n**Data sources**\n- `haul_vehicles` \u2014 daily operational records: loads, payload tons, cycle time, fuel\n- `sensor_readings` \u2014 daily telemetry: engine temp, tire pressure, hydraulics, health score, alert level\n- `failure_events` \u2014 monthly failure events with downtime, repair cost, RUL, 30-day failure probability",
