  "genie_instructions": "DOMAIN CONTEXT\nThis space supports Haul Vehicle Asset Health for a surface mining operation running 20 ultra-class haul trucks (Cat 797F, Komatsu 930E, Liebherr T284, Hitachi EH5000, BelAZ 75710, Cat 794AC) across four pits. Stakeholders include the Mine Manager (availability, cycle time, loads completed), Fleet Manager (alerts, sensor anomalies, tire and engine health), Reliability VP (MTBF, RUL, failure-type Pareto), and CFO (repair cost, unplanned downtime $ impact, capex deferral).\n\nMETRIC DEFINITIONS\n- Mechanical availability proxy = vehicles not in Critical alert; benchmark 85-92% for ultra-class trucks\n- Daily payload tons = payload_tons (total per truck-day, 100-400 ton range); loads_completed = trips per day\n- Cycle time = cycle_time_minutes; healthy ~22-30 min for typical 5km hauls\n- Fleet health score = AVG(health_score) on sensor_readings (0-100)\n- Alert level = alert_level on sensor_readings (Normal / Caution / Warning / Critical)\n- MTBF proxy = operating hours between failure_events; benchmark 200-400 hrs depending on model\n- RUL = rul_days on failure_events (component changeout horizon)\n- 30-day failure probability = failure_probability_pct on failure_events (>25% = high risk)\n- Engine temp = engine_temp_celsius; >100C indicates overheating risk\n\nQUERY GUIDANCE\n- ALWAYS prefer metric views with MEASURE() syntax for aggregations.\n  - health_monthly (source: sensor_readings) \u2014 dims: reading_date, vehicle_model, pit, alert_level; measures: avg_health_score, avg_engine_temp, vehicle_count, critical_count, reading_count, total_tire_pressure_psi, total_hydraulic_pressure_bar, max_engine_temp_celsius.\n  - failure_monthly (source: failure_events) \u2014 dims: event_month, vehicle_model, pit, failure_type; measures: total_downtime, total_repair_cost, avg_rul, failure_count, high_risk_count, unique_vehicle_count, max_downtime_hours.\n- Use GROUP BY ALL with MEASURE() queries.\n- For monthly trends, always wrap the date in DATE_TRUNC('month', <date_col>).\n- For \"Top X\" requests, return LIMIT 10 unless the user specifies otherwise.\n- Query base tables directly only when needing columns not exposed by metric views (e.g. vehicle_id, vehicle_name, payload_tons, fuel_liters, repair_cost_usd, failure_probability_pct).\n- When the user's phrasing matches a SQL snippet display name (filters, expressions, or measures), prefer that snippet.",
  "sample_questions": [
    "Show monthly fleet health score trend by vehicle model for the trailing 12 months.",
    "Which 10 haul trucks have the highest 30-day failure probability right now, and what is each one's RUL?",
    "Top 10 vehicle models by total unplanned downtime hours this year \u2014 rank by lost production impact.",
    "How has total repair cost trended month-over-month by failure type across the fleet?",
    "Which pits have the most Critical alerts in the last 90 days, and which vehicle models are driving them?",
    "What is the average daily payload by vehicle model across the fleet?",
    "Top 10 vehicles by repair cost over the last 6 months \u2014 and what failure types are most common on each?"
  ],
  "example_sqls": [
    {
      "question": "How many distinct snapshots appeared each month?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT DATE_TRUNC('month', reading_date) AS month, COUNT(DISTINCT snapshot) AS distinct_count",
        "FROM {fqn}.sensor_readings",
        "GROUP BY 1",
        "ORDER BY 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has average engine temperature c trended by month?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT reading_date, MEASURE(avg_engine_temp) AS avg_engine_temp",
        "FROM {fqn}.health_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY reading_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How many distinct forecasts appeared each month?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT DATE_TRUNC('month', event_month) AS month, COUNT(DISTINCT forecast) AS distinct_count",
        "FROM {fqn}.failure_events",
        "GROUP BY 1",
        "ORDER BY 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has high risk count changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT event_month, MEASURE(high_risk_count) AS high_risk_count",
        "FROM {fqn}.failure_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY event_month"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the trend of total loads completed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT record_date, SUM(loads_completed) AS total_loads_completed",
        "FROM {fqn}.haul_vehicles",
        "GROUP BY record_date ORDER BY record_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the trend of total engine temperature c over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT reading_date, SUM(engine_temp_celsius) AS total_engine_temp_celsius",
        "FROM {fqn}.sensor_readings",
        "GROUP BY reading_date ORDER BY reading_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has the average 30-day failure probability changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT event_month, AVG(failure_probability_pct) AS avg_failure_probability_pct",
        "FROM {fqn}.failure_events",
        "GROUP BY event_month ORDER BY event_month"
      ]
    }
  ],
